 "notes": [
  "Phase 4 (Sep 29 2026, Colab Enterprise L4 24 GB, us-east4): QLoRA (4-bit nf4, r=16, alpha=32, dropout 0.05, all q/k/v/o/gate/up/down projections; lr 1e-4 warmup+linear decay, 2 epochs, grad-accum 8, TRAIN_TOKENS 2400, answer-only loss on 'Yes'/'No' + end-of-turn) on Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct, CVE-grouped 5-fold: each fold's adapter is trained on ~366 samples and scored on the ~92 held-out samples; pooled held-out scores are bootstrapped (5000 resamples over pairs).",
  "untuned = the stock Instruct model on the same samples (mouth) and a probe on its own hidden states with the same folds (best layer chosen inside the training fold). This is the first probe on the Instruct checkpoint itself (0.737) \u2014 the frozen BASE probe from Phase 1.5 is 0.796.",
  "tuned.probe = probe on the fine-tuned model's hidden states (layer chosen by inner CV on the training fold; layers per fold listed). Control numbers for the tuned model average each control pair's outcome over the five fold-models before bootstrapping.",
  "Training-loss floor ~0.34 per answer token: the end-of-turn token is learned (~0), the Yes/No token stays near ln 2 = 0.693 on the training folds themselves -> the adapter learned the answer format and the label marginal, not the code->label mapping. Tuned P(yes) spans 0.35-0.68 with only 19 distinct values across the 460 samples; P(yes) 0.488 on vulnerable vs 0.477 on fixed twins; pair outcomes 125 wins / 2 ties / 101 losses.",
  "Run notes: first execution of cell 8 hit CUDA OOM (a stale kernel from the xmodel_qwen25_7b notebook held 9.6 GB of the card for the whole run, and free() had not released the untuned model); fixed by cells 7b-7f and by computing the loss from answer-only logits (logits_to_keep) instead of labels= (mathematically identical). See the markdown notes in notebooks/phase4_finetune_qwen25coder7b.ipynb.",
  "Not a temporal split: tuned.mouth.post2024 is the pooled held-out score restricted to the 56 2024+ pairs (0.482 [0.357,0.607])."
